# Changelog (released versions are frozen)

[CHANGELOG.md](CHANGELOG.md) follows Keep a Changelog. Dated `## [x.y.z]`
sections are **immutable**.

**CHANGELOG = product. Website ≠ product.** Do not add, date, or “complete
a release” with `website/**` notes (Pages, Starlight, cookies/consent,
articles chrome, site CSS). Leave Unreleased empty if the train only
has site work.

Product is the `cicerone` package: job, serve, dashboard app, events, I/O,
CLI, config, models.

## Do

- Put new notes only under `## [Unreleased]` on the train you are
  targeting (patch on `main`, minor on `release/X.Y.0`).
- Short bullets for **this** product change. Do not re-tell older releases.

## Do not

- Changelog the website. Ever.
- Edit, rewrite, move, or “clarify” any `## [x.y.z] - YYYY-MM-DD` section.
- Expand Unreleased bullets so they re-document a shipped version
  (e.g. do not narrate 0.5.0 lock behavior inside a later HA note).
- Backport Unreleased items into an already-tagged release section.
